commit f0a2fca9242f1308b6e772d0ba6dfcf56c58fb24
Author: Christie Hubley <christie@tinkerartstudio.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 23:04:34 2026 -0600

    fix: copied-camp review — implementation review round 1 (Codex + Claude)
    
    Codex: "not safe" — a camp could be marked reviewed after its latest grid change silently failed to
    save. Verified and fixed, with the rest:
    
    - autoSaveCurriculum records whether it failed; Mark reviewed refuses (and says why) when the flushed
      auto-save failed (Codex 2)
    - while Mark reviewed waits for the pending auto-save, the editor can't be closed, re-opened on another
      camp, or Saved — the queued auto-save reads the open form (Codex 1)
    - closeModal: the generic × / backdrop handlers closed the curriculum editor even mid-Save —
      pre-existing, it made the Save lock's "editor stays" guard dead; found by the new test
    - Save re-renders the review band when it ends (a button drawn mid-save stayed disabled) (Claude 3);
      opening the editor resets a stale in-flight flag and the auto-save failure flag (Claude 4)
    - staff/prep: co-teachers show as a count when names can't be read, not raw uids (Claude 2)
    - Lesson Plans: the badge sits with the status badge and wraps (Claude 1)
    - tests: flush failure, review-write failure (band/card/count stay unreviewed), close refused while
      flushing, the read-only stylesheet really hides the button (computed style), carry-forward asserts
      the WRITTEN copy has no reviewedAt/reviewedBy (Codex 4); seedCopied comment/fields (Claude 7)
    
    Not taken: escaping camp names in the other tabs (pre-existing, untouched here — Claude 9); dropping
    the blocks check from campReviewState (the round-1 plan review asked for it; carry-forward never
    writes a copy without blocks — Claude 5).
    
    e2e 143/143; carry-forward 27; season 57; migration 32; data-safety 11; completeness clean.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

